      "topic": "恢复并校验全部 bzip2 拼接成员，统一限制总输出并保留固件尾随数据兼容",
      "title": "Recover every concatenated bzip2 member within one output budget (R3.12)",
      "body": "## Problem\n\nThe existing bzip2 decoder returns the first member of a concatenated stream. Recovery can silently omit later content, accept a damaged later member, or apply the output budget only to the first member. ZIP method 12 uses the same public decoder.\n\n## Change\n\n- Decode each member in order with one shared bounded output sink, including empty members.\n- Check each member's block and combined checksums and reject unfinished members instead of returning the earlier valid prefix.\n- Keep firmware-carving compatibility with non-member bytes after a complete stream. Invalid initial input and a truncated next-member header remain errors.\n- Use the safe `bzip2::bufread::BzDecoder` interface, whose returned input exposes the exact remaining bytes. The previous `bzip2-rs` interface did not expose unused buffered input.\n- Resolve `bzip2 0.6.1` with its default pure Rust `libbz2-rs-sys 0.2.6` backend. No C backend is enabled. Cargo adds only these two packages and removes the old decoder and its now-unused `tinyvec` leaf dependency; existing package versions do not change.\n\nThe public result/error types and output limit are unchanged. Concatenated streams are part of the [bzip2 format's supported behavior](https://sourceware.org/bzip2/manual/manual.html).\n\n## Validation\n\nThe [original-production comparison](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43062392709/job/130668146515) runs native `bzip2 -dc` 1.0.8 on 34 independently generated inputs and compares complete output bytes or error results, including the caller's total output budget. Original production at `3ce1ce9` disagrees in **17 cases**.\n\nThe [fixed preparation and complete gates](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43063316908/job/130671455264) regenerate the exact same 34 inputs, assert their matrix SHA-256, and find **zero differences**. Cases include multiple and empty members, Unicode/binary data, compression levels 1 and 9, a 225,900-byte multi-block payload, block/combined checksum damage in later members, incomplete headers and bodies, trailing non-member bytes, and exact/exceeded total budgets.\n\nTen checked-in regression groups cover those boundaries and complete ZIP method-12 recovery, including the ZIP member's own CRC and output budget. They give **6 failures and 4 passing controls** on the unchanged production code, and **10 passing groups** after the change. Every nonempty incomplete prefix of a later member is checked.\n\nThe complete formats and engine suites pass **2,396 tests, 0 failures, 17 existing ignored tests** across 227 test/doc targets. Rust 1.99 formatting, strict all-target Clippy for both crates, layer/lock/secret checks, and all five L0-L2 WebAssembly builds pass.\n\n[Published-source verification](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43066011812/job/130681025957) checks final head `c16fae5391484a753a3a5bd13697c0dc6efb4967` against the exact source, regression file, manifest and Cargo-generated lockfile from the successful preparation job. It verifies the public claim parent, the seven-file scope, formatting and repository contracts. The final documentation does not require a duplicate full test run.\n\n## Validation history and scope\n\nThe first comparison used Python's `bz2.decompress`, which can swallow an error in a later member as trailing data. The final integrity oracle is the actual native CLI exit status, with complete-byte comparisons; this lesson is recorded in pitfalls. Python 3.12.3 generates the compressed inputs.\n\nThe initial native-comparison run linked above completed the negative controls but failed a validation-only dependency allowlist because it had not accounted for the removed decoder's unused `tinyvec` dependency. The subsequent gate checks the exact two removals and two additions; no product assertion was weakened.\n\nChecked the decoder history and all-state bzip2/bz2 PR searches. #1374 added ZIP bzip2/XZ extraction through the existing decoder; this fixes complete bzip2 member recovery itself. No native Windows run, external firmware corpus, or performance improvement is claimed. The public R3.12 claim preceded implementation.\n",
